然后我的角色说，什么？

1424
01:01:31.160 --> 01:01:34.060
And he's like, Sparkles, the white one, is dead.
他说，斯帕克尔斯，那只白色的猫，死了。

1425
01:01:34.420 --> 01:01:35.920
Yeah, he gets the name wrong.
没错，他把名字叫错了。

1426
01:01:36.120 --> 01:01:36.800
It's bad.
太糟糕了。

1427
01:01:36.880 --> 01:01:37.600
It is bad.
确实很糟糕。

1428
01:01:37.840 --> 01:01:39.340
This will not end well.
这事儿没法善终。

1429
01:01:39.340 --> 01:01:46.300
Angela, you get so very immediately emotional, and not in a funny way.
安吉拉，你立刻就变得非常情绪化，而且不是那种搞笑的方式。

1430
01:01:46.480 --> 01:01:53.580
Like, this is one of the ways that our show allowed characters to be real people, because
这是我们剧集让角色成为真实人物的方式之一，因为

1431
01:01:54.540 --> 01:02:01.640
Angela, the character, really loved her cat, and she is heartbroken, and you see that real
安吉拉这个角色真的很爱她的猫，她心碎了，你在这里看到了你角色

1432
01:02:01.640 --> 01:02:03.400
pain here from your character.
真实的痛苦。

1433
01:02:03.600 --> 01:02:05.720
How did you gear up for this scene?
你是如何为这一幕做准备的？

1434
01:02:05.720 --> 01:02:12.460
Well, Greg told me, he said, you know, Angela Martin, hearing this news will be devastated.
格雷格告诉我，他说，你知道，安吉拉·马丁听到这个消息会崩溃的。

1435
01:02:13.060 --> 01:02:20.640
And I need you to play out the beats of hearing news that kind of destroys you in the moment.
我需要你表现出听到那种瞬间摧毁你的消息时的心路历程。

1436
01:02:20.820 --> 01:02:25.580
You know, and I feel like we've all had moments in our lives where we've gotten that phone call
你知道，我觉得我们生活中都有过那种时刻，就是接到电话

1437
01:02:25.580 --> 01:02:27.820
with some bad news, you know, unfortunately.
听到坏消息的时候，你知道，不幸的是。

1438
01:02:28.280 --> 01:02:35.660
And I just sort of thought about a few of those moments where, you know, at first,
我当时就想到了那几个时刻，你知道，起初，

1439
01:02:35.720 --> 01:02:39.720
you're just in total shock, where you're not really sure what you heard.
你完全处于震惊之中，甚至不确定自己听到了什么。

1440
01:02:40.540 --> 01:02:40.980
Yeah.
是啊。

1441
01:02:41.120 --> 01:02:44.680
And then it's like someone slaps you in the face with the information.
然后就像有人当面给了你一记耳光，让你清醒地意识到这个消息。

1442
01:02:45.960 --> 01:02:49.280
And then you're trying to make sense of it, but you can't make sense of it.
接着你试图去理解它，但你根本无法理解。

1443
01:02:49.880 --> 01:02:52.740
It's the unthinkable, and it doesn't make sense.
那是不可思议的事，根本说不通。

1444
01:02:53.040 --> 01:02:55.020
And your body is doing all of that.
你的身体正在经历这一切。

1445
01:02:55.300 --> 01:02:56.140
You're in shock.
你处于震惊中。

1446
01:02:56.140 --> 01:02:57.100
You're sad.
你很悲伤。

1447
01:02:57.540 --> 01:03:01.480
Your body, your mind is trying to make it right, but you can't make it right.
你的身体、你的大脑都在试图让一切恢复正常，但你无法挽回。

1448
01:03:01.660 --> 01:03:02.740
You can't figure it out.
你无法想通。

1449
01:03:02.880 --> 01:03:04.380
You don't understand why it happened.
你不明白为什么会发生这种事。

1450
01:03:04.860 --> 01:03:08.340
And I was just trying to process through all of that.
我当时只是试图去消化这一切。

1451
01:03:08.800 --> 01:03:11.700
And yeah, that's what I did.
没错，我就是这么做的。

1452
01:03:11.860 --> 01:03:14.020
Did you have to do a lot of takes of that scene?
那场戏你拍了很多遍吗？

1453
01:03:14.020 --> 01:03:14.660
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

1454
01:03:14.980 --> 01:03:15.900
No, I didn't.
不，我没拍很多遍。

1455
01:03:15.900 --> 01:03:17.220
I was thankful for that.
对此我很庆幸。

1456
01:03:17.600 --> 01:03:20.400
In the next scene, your character is still crying.
在下一场戏里，你的角色还在哭。

1457
01:03:20.580 --> 01:03:22.500
She's standing at reception with Pam.
她正和帕姆站在接待处。

1458
01:03:22.500 --> 01:03:26.780
And you look like you've been crying for a long time.
而且你看上去已经哭了很久了。

1459
01:03:27.260 --> 01:03:32.520
What did you do to get there, to start the scene in a place like that?
你是怎么进入状态的，让自己在开拍时就处于那种情绪中？

1460
01:03:32.600 --> 01:03:33.740
You know, I'm chatty.
你知道，我这人很爱聊天。

1461
01:03:33.860 --> 01:03:38.640
So my instinct would be, I'm standing by reception with you, would be to be hanging out, you know,
所以我的本能反应是，既然和你一起站在接待处，就会想闲聊几句，你知道的，

1462
01:03:38.940 --> 01:03:40.100
being part of the bullpen.
融入到办公室的氛围里。

1463
01:03:40.100 --> 01:03:45.380
And so one of the things I did was I went around the corner by the elevators by myself in between
所以我采取的方法之一是，在拍摄间隙，我独自走到电梯拐角处，

1464
01:03:45.380 --> 01:03:47.080
takes, and I did not hang out.
不去和别人闲聊。

1465
01:03:47.200 --> 01:03:50.340
And I just tried to stay in sort of that sad space.
我只是努力让自己待在那种悲伤的情绪里。

1466
01:03:51.860 --> 01:03:59.540
And also the makeup department, they wanted my eyes to really look like I had bawled my eyes out.
而且化妆部门也希望我的眼睛看起来真的像是大哭过一场。

1467
01:03:59.620 --> 01:04:00.560
And they did.
他们确实做到了。

1468
01:04:00.560 --> 01:04:04.000
So I had to get myself back in that emotional place and get sad again.
所以我必须让自己回到那种情绪中，重新变得悲伤起来。

1469
01:04:04.580 --> 01:04:11.240
And also the makeup department, Kenneth Paul, who did my makeup, did like this type of eyeliner
另外，负责给我化妆的肯尼斯·保罗，他用了一种眼线，

1470
01:04:11.240 --> 01:04:16.240
that really made the inside, it was like in the inside of your eye, reddish pink.
那种眼线真的让我的眼内侧看起来红红粉粉的。

1471
01:04:16.540 --> 01:04:21.120
So my eyes looked the part, and then emotionally I got there.
所以我的眼睛看起来很到位，然后在情绪上我也进入了状态。

1472
01:04:22.080 --> 01:04:25.760
Your eyes looked like you had three margaritas yesterday.
你的眼睛看起来就像昨天喝了三杯玛格丽特一样。

1473
01:04:27.020 --> 01:04:28.260
That's what you look like.
你看起来就是那样。

1474
01:04:28.260 --> 01:04:31.740
Actually, that should have been my prep instead of eyeliner and sad thoughts.
其实，我当初应该用这个方法来准备，而不是靠眼线和悲伤的念头。

1475
01:04:32.620 --> 01:04:38.920
No, what happened was Laverne just showed Kenneth Paul a picture of me from the previous day
不，其实是拉弗恩给肯尼斯·保罗看了我前一天的一张照片，

1476
01:04:38.920 --> 01:04:40.640
and was like, make her look like that.
然后说，让她看起来像那样就行。

1477
01:04:41.020 --> 01:04:45.740
No, but in all seriousness, Angela, when I was watching these series of scenes where your character
不开玩笑了，安吉拉，当我看到这一系列戏份时，你的角色

1478
01:04:45.740 --> 01:04:53.300
is really, really devastated over the death of Sprinkles, I was just so beyond impressed
因为斯普林克尔斯的死而感到非常非常崩溃，我真的对你的表演、你的戏路和你的真实感印象深刻。

1479
01:04:53.300 --> 01:04:58.000
with your performance and your range and your believability.
这简直太棒了，非常出色的表演。

1480
01:04:58.440 --> 01:05:02.060
It was just, this is just great, great work.
这真的很棒，非常棒的工作。

1481
01:05:02.280 --> 01:05:03.220
Aw, thanks.
噢，谢谢。

1482
01:05:03.300 --> 01:05:04.640
I appreciate that.
我很感激。

1483
01:05:04.860 --> 01:05:10.380
I really appreciated Greg writing the storyline for me, and I got to do all these things,
我真的很感谢格雷格为我写了这个故事线，让我有机会去尝试所有这些表演，

1484
01:05:10.480 --> 01:05:17.120
you know, and, you know, his take as a director was always to try to keep it as honest as possible.
你知道，作为导演，他一贯的方针就是尽量保持真实。

1485
01:05:17.800 --> 01:05:18.460
Yeah.
是的。

1486
01:05:19.400 --> 01:05:20.000
Yeah.
没错。

1487
01:05:20.000 --> 01:05:26.900
Well, there's another really great moment in this scene, and we actually had a fan write in.
嗯，这一幕里还有另一个非常棒的时刻，其实有位粉丝写信提到了。

1488
01:05:27.120 --> 01:05:28.500
Katie Harwick said,
凯蒂·哈威克说，

1489
01:05:28.500 --> 01:05:34.180
I think we need to give a shout-out to Michael when Angela's cat dies.
我觉得我们得给安吉拉的猫死掉时迈克尔的表现点个赞。

1490
01:05:34.600 --> 01:05:39.080
Not only did he know her name, but he was overcome with grief.
他不仅知道猫的名字，而且还悲痛欲绝。

1491
01:05:39.240 --> 01:05:44.160
He cares so much for his employees, and it was just such a sweet moment to me.
他非常关心他的员工，对我来说，那真是一个非常暖心的时刻。

1492
01:05:44.360 --> 01:05:51.220
But I do have to ask, do you think he was truly sad, or did he just see this as a distraction
但我必须问一下，你觉得他是真的难过，还是仅仅把这看作是一个转移注意力的机会，

1493
01:05:51.220 --> 01:05:54.000
from hitting Meredith that everyone could talk about instead?
好让大家不再谈论他撞到梅雷迪斯的事？

1494
01:05:54.000 --> 01:05:58.820
Instead, I personally think he was very distraught about sprinkles.
相反，我个人认为他是真的为斯普林克尔斯感到难过。

1495
01:05:59.120 --> 01:06:00.160
Well, I agree.
嗯，我同意。

1496
01:06:00.460 --> 01:06:06.380
This happens at 12 minutes, 41 seconds, and it is one of my favorite endearing moments of Michael.
这一幕发生在12分41秒，这是我最喜欢的迈克尔展现温情的时刻之一。

1497
01:06:06.520 --> 01:06:10.540
Now, maybe because it's personal for me, because, you know, I played Angela Martin.
也许是因为这对我来说很私人，毕竟，你知道，我扮演的是安吉拉·马丁。

1498
01:06:10.640 --> 01:06:12.140
I knew how much she loved her cats.
我知道她有多爱她的猫。

1499
01:06:12.480 --> 01:06:18.680
But Michael, it's like that moment when the trick-or-treaters come to his house, and you see his joy.
但迈克尔，这就像当不给糖就捣蛋的孩子来到他家时，你看到他流露出的那种喜悦。

1500
01:06:18.940 --> 01:06:22.700
It's like that moment when he shows up to Pam's art show.
这就像他出现在帕姆的艺术展上时的那一刻一样。

1501
01:06:23.240 --> 01:06:23.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1502
01:06:23.680 --> 01:06:27.280
Michael really saw these people as his family.
迈克尔真的把这些人当成了他的家人。

1503
01:06:27.540 --> 01:06:30.220
So Michael knew Angela's love of sprinkles.
所以迈克尔知道安吉拉有多喜欢“糖针”。

1504
01:06:30.380 --> 01:06:31.280
Of course he did.
他当然知道。

1505
01:06:31.720 --> 01:06:32.280
Yeah.
是啊。

1506
01:06:32.280 --> 01:06:35.060
And he was gutted to hear that sprinkles died.
听说“糖针”死了，他难过极了。

1507
01:06:35.240 --> 01:06:39.920
The way he puts his hand up to his face, and he kind of collapses into the wall, and he's like,
他把手捂在脸上，整个人瘫倒在墙上，然后他说，

1508
01:06:40.480 --> 01:06:41.480
oh, shoot.
噢，天哪。

1509
01:06:41.880 --> 01:06:43.520
I'm sorry, Angela.
我很抱歉，安吉拉。

1510
01:06:43.940 --> 01:06:46.360
I mean, could it get any worse?
我是说，还能有比这更糟的事吗？

1511
01:06:47.060 --> 01:06:48.560
He's feeling all of that.
他感同身受。

1512
01:06:48.740 --> 01:06:50.000
He really feels bad.
他真的感到很难过。

1513
01:06:50.000 --> 01:06:57.040
And now he gets sprinkles' name right the first time, and then he makes a big speech and calls her prinkles.
现在他第一次就把“糖针”的名字叫对了，结果发表长篇大论时又管它叫“普林克”。

1514
01:06:57.340 --> 01:06:57.980
So, you know.
所以，你知道的。

1515
01:06:58.120 --> 01:06:58.600
He does.
他确实是这样。

1516
01:06:59.280 --> 01:07:00.080
That's right.
没错。

1517
01:07:00.340 --> 01:07:04.500
He says, so many bad things have happened today.
他说，今天发生了太多糟糕的事情。

1518
01:07:04.500 --> 01:07:10.740
The computer crashes from porn, merit of this accident, and now prinkles.
电脑因为看色情片死机，发生了这起事故，现在又是“普林克”。

1519
01:07:10.740 --> 01:07:11.820
We're cursed.
我们被诅咒了。

1520
01:07:12.180 --> 01:07:13.660
This seals the deal.
这下彻底完了。

1521
01:07:14.060 --> 01:07:15.840
To him, that's it.
对他来说，就是这样。

1522
01:07:15.940 --> 01:07:20.080
The office is cursed, and now he's got to figure out how to break this curse.
办公室被诅咒了，现在他得想办法破除这个诅咒。

1523
01:07:20.600 --> 01:07:24.880
Yes, but he does say, I'm not superstitious, but I am a little stitious.
没错，但他确实说了，“我不迷信，但我有点迷信”。

1524
01:07:25.860 --> 01:07:28.320
It's like he thinks they're two separate words.
就好像他觉得这是两个独立的词一样。

1525
01:07:28.640 --> 01:07:34.360
Well, we had a fan question about that line from Jessica Williard and Lauren Corwin.
嗯，我们收到过杰西卡·威利亚德和劳伦·科温关于那句台词的粉丝提问。

1526
01:07:34.800 --> 01:07:38.200
They said, that line makes me laugh every time.
她们说，那句台词每次都让我大笑。

1527
01:07:39.040 --> 01:07:40.720
Who wrote this joke?
这个笑话是谁写的？

1528
01:07:40.920 --> 01:07:42.100
I was curious, too.
我也很好奇。

1529
01:07:42.220 --> 01:07:43.040
Did you find out?
你查到了吗？

1530
01:07:43.440 --> 01:07:44.140
I did.
查到了。

1531
01:07:44.380 --> 01:07:45.800
It was Gene Stepnitzky.
是吉恩·斯蒂普尼茨基写的。

1532
01:07:46.020 --> 01:07:47.440
Gene, hilarious.
吉恩，太搞笑了。

1533
01:07:48.140 --> 01:07:52.560
Yeah, I asked Greg, and he said, I'm pretty sure it was Gene or Lee.
是啊，我问了格雷格，他说，我挺确定是吉恩或者李写的。

1534
01:07:52.560 --> 01:07:54.280
I reached out to those guys.
我联系了他们。

1535
01:07:54.520 --> 01:07:56.600
Gene said, yes, it was me.
吉恩说，是的，是我写的。

1536
01:07:56.820 --> 01:07:57.500
He remembers.
他记得。

1537
01:07:57.800 --> 01:08:04.280
They were in a group, and this talking head leads to a commercial break, and they needed
当时他们在一个小组里，这段采访片段之后要进广告，他们需要

1538
01:08:04.280 --> 01:08:04.820
a button.
一个结尾。

1539
01:08:05.040 --> 01:08:10.340
They needed a little button at the end of this talking head so that they could go to commercial,
他们需要在这段采访结束时加个小尾巴，好让他们进入广告，

1540
01:08:10.460 --> 01:08:15.000
and he said they were just trying to come up with something, and all of a sudden, he
他说他们当时就在想点子，突然间，他

1541
01:08:15.000 --> 01:08:16.860
said, he shouted out, I've got it.
喊道，我想到了。

1542
01:08:17.080 --> 01:08:20.280
This might be stupid, but how about this?
这可能很蠢，但这个怎么样？

1543
01:08:20.280 --> 01:08:24.200
Yes, and he pitched that line, and it is so genius.
是的，他提出了那句台词，真是天才之作。

1544
01:08:24.440 --> 01:08:28.120
It is such a good line, and I hear that line quoted all the time.
那真是一句好台词，我经常听到有人引用它。

1545
01:08:28.240 --> 01:08:30.160
It is a Michael Scott classic line.
这是迈克尔·斯科特的经典台词。

1546
01:08:30.520 --> 01:08:31.340
It is.
确实。

1547
01:08:31.440 --> 01:08:32.000
It's true.
没错。

1548
01:08:32.780 --> 01:08:38.400
Well, speaking of classic Michael Scott, we're now going to move into one of Michael's conference
说到迈克尔·斯科特的经典，我们现在要进入迈克尔的一场会议室

1549
01:08:38.400 --> 01:08:39.160
room meetings.
会议了。

1550
01:08:39.520 --> 01:08:41.900
This is an epic conference room meeting.
这是一场史诗级的会议室会议。

1551
01:08:42.080 --> 01:08:44.500
We were in this conference room all freaking day.
我们整整一天都待在这个会议室里。

1552
01:08:44.500 --> 01:08:46.260
Anyway, we got loopy.
总之，我们都变得有点神志不清了。

1553
01:08:46.420 --> 01:08:47.240
We got punchy.
我们都变得有些亢奋。

1554
01:08:47.360 --> 01:08:49.700
I'm going to tell you where we flat out lost it.
我要告诉你们我们彻底失控的地方。

1555
01:08:50.120 --> 01:08:51.260
It's so good.
真的太精彩了。

1556
01:08:51.680 --> 01:08:51.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1557
01:08:52.000 --> 01:08:59.180
I also remember that they very specifically did not seat Jim and Pam next to one another.
我还记得他们特意没有让吉姆和帕姆坐在一起。

1558
01:08:59.380 --> 01:09:05.620
This was part of Jim and Pam's supposed way of deflecting that we're dating.
这是吉姆和帕姆所谓的掩盖我们在约会的方法的一部分。

1559
01:09:06.340 --> 01:09:06.860
Yeah.
是啊。

1560
01:09:07.400 --> 01:09:12.120
And I remember that you have to just be sad and kind of cry through this scene, and that
我记得你必须一直保持悲伤，在这一幕里哭出来，而我

1561
01:09:12.120 --> 01:09:17.000
I didn't want to chat you up too much because I knew you had to stay in that space.
我不想跟你聊太多，因为我知道你必须保持那种情绪状态。

1562
01:09:17.200 --> 01:09:18.060
And I did.
我确实做到了。

1563
01:09:18.220 --> 01:09:18.800
I did.
我确实做到了。

1564
01:09:19.320 --> 01:09:23.900
I really stayed sad until the end when Steve made me break into laughter.
我一直保持着悲伤，直到最后史蒂夫让我破功大笑。

1565
01:09:24.160 --> 01:09:26.700
So Michael in the scene is questioning his employees.
所以迈克尔在这一幕里审问他的员工。

1566
01:09:26.980 --> 01:09:30.440
He feels like someone must have done something to get this curse, right?
他觉得肯定有人做了什么事才招致了这个诅咒，对吧？

1567
01:09:30.440 --> 01:09:34.080
Like, have they violated an ancient Indian burial ground?
比如，他们是不是冒犯了古老的印第安墓地？

1568
01:09:34.380 --> 01:09:39.800
And then, you know, he wants to know what everyone's religious beliefs are, which Toby
然后，你知道，他想知道每个人的宗教信仰是什么，托比就

1569
01:09:39.800 --> 01:09:42.560
says, Michael, we can't, you can't do that.
说，迈克尔，我们不能，你不能那样做。

1570
01:09:42.720 --> 01:09:43.740
You can't discuss that.
你不能讨论那个。

1571
01:09:43.960 --> 01:09:47.160
Michael calls Toby Satan repeatedly in the scene.
迈克尔在这一幕里反复称呼托比为撒旦。

1572
01:09:47.820 --> 01:09:50.300
One, because he won a week of free pizza.
第一，因为他赢了一周的免费披萨。

1573
01:09:50.420 --> 01:09:51.800
So he's like, I don't think there's a curse.
所以他说，我不觉得有什么诅咒。

1574
01:09:51.980 --> 01:09:53.300
And Michael's like, okay, Satan.
迈克尔就说，好吧，撒旦。

1575
01:09:53.800 --> 01:09:55.440
So he goes around the room.
于是他在房间里转了一圈。

1576
01:09:55.620 --> 01:09:57.900
Pam and Daryl are both Presbyterians.
帕姆和达里尔都是长老会教徒。

1577
01:09:58.200 --> 01:09:58.820
They high five.
他们击了个掌。

1578
01:10:00.440 --> 01:10:04.080
There's this great line where she says, I'm a Lutheran and Bob is a Unitarian.
有一句很棒的台词是她说，我是路德教徒，鲍勃是唯一神教派教徒。

1579
01:10:04.360 --> 01:10:05.640
Keeps things spicy.
生活总得有点情趣。

1580
01:10:06.700 --> 01:10:07.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1581
01:10:07.700 --> 01:10:11.300
Creed said he's been a follower in a cult and a leader in a cult.
克里德说他当过邪教的追随者，也当过邪教的领袖。

1582
01:10:11.500 --> 01:10:14.020
The followers have more fun, but the leaders make more money.
追随者更有趣，但领袖赚得更多。

1583
01:10:14.280 --> 01:10:19.640
But Michael has decided he thinks maybe we should do an animal sacrifice.
但迈克尔决定他认为也许我们应该进行一次动物祭祀。

1584
01:10:20.020 --> 01:10:20.380
Yes.
是的。

1585
01:10:20.500 --> 01:10:20.720
You know?
你知道吗？

1586
01:10:20.840 --> 01:10:21.800
That's going to do it.
那样应该就行了。

1587
01:10:21.840 --> 01:10:22.480
Maybe that would help.
也许那会有帮助。

1588
01:10:22.660 --> 01:10:22.860
Yeah.
是啊。

1589
01:10:23.000 --> 01:10:23.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1590
01:10:23.600 --> 01:10:29.100
And then he starts naming animals, but they don't exiSt.
然后他开始列举动物，但它们根本不存在。

1591
01:10:29.100 --> 01:10:30.700
I wrote them down.
我把它们记下来了。

1592
01:10:30.920 --> 01:10:39.620
He suggests that we sacrifice an animal that has the body of a walrus and the head of a sea lion.
他建议我们祭祀一种长着海象身体和海狮脑袋的动物。

1593
01:10:49.180 --> 01:10:59.640
Maybe one that has the head of a monkey with the antlers of a reindeer and the body of a porcupine.
也许是那种长着猴子脑袋、驯鹿鹿角和豪猪身体的动物。

1594
01:10:59.640 --> 01:11:04.800
Okay, Jenna, when Steve started this runner, they just let him go.
好吧，珍娜，当史蒂夫开始这个梗的时候，他们就让他自由发挥了。

1595
01:11:05.040 --> 01:11:05.940
Do you remember this?
你还记得吗？

1596
01:11:06.160 --> 01:11:06.340
Yes.
记得。

1597
01:11:06.400 --> 01:11:10.240
He just started improvising different animal combinations.
他开始即兴编造各种动物组合。

1598
01:11:10.600 --> 01:11:11.020
Yes.
是的。

1599
01:11:11.020 --> 01:11:13.620
We didn't know what was going to come out of the guy's mouth.
我们根本不知道这家伙嘴里会蹦出什么来。

1600
01:11:13.620 --> 01:11:18.180
We all started dropping like flies, cracking up.
我们所有人都笑得东倒西歪，彻底破功了。

1601
01:11:18.300 --> 01:11:21.640
And the other thing is, he would say it with such seriousness.
还有一点是，他说话时那种一本正经的样子。

1602
01:11:22.120 --> 01:11:27.300
And this was the comedy killer, the long pauses.
最搞笑的地方就在于此，那些长长的停顿。

1603
01:11:27.580 --> 01:11:33.200
He takes such a long pause before he says, body of a porcupine?
他在说出“豪猪的身体”之前，停顿了那么久？

1604
01:11:33.680 --> 01:11:34.280
Yes.
没错。

1605
01:11:34.500 --> 01:11:35.380
We were on the floor.
我们当时都笑趴下了。

1606
01:11:35.560 --> 01:11:36.920
We were on the floor.
我们都笑得东倒西歪。

1607
01:11:37.140 --> 01:11:42.700
I am not in any background shots while he's doing these animal combinations because I couldn't keep it together.
他在做这些动物组合表演时，我没出现在任何背景镜头里，因为我根本憋不住笑。

1608
01:11:43.340 --> 01:11:49.000
And at 18 minutes, 11 seconds, you can see Craig Robinson covering his face.
在18分11秒的时候，你可以看到克雷格·罗宾逊在捂着脸。

1609
01:11:49.380 --> 01:11:50.420
I saw it.
我看到了。

1610
01:11:50.780 --> 01:11:51.960
I remember that.
我记得那一幕。

1611
01:11:52.580 --> 01:11:54.600
We were losing it.
我们当时都快失控了。

1612
01:11:55.280 --> 01:11:57.920
It was so funny.
太好笑了。

1613
01:11:58.100 --> 01:12:00.700
And they let him go for a long time.
而且他们让他演了很久。

1614
01:12:01.220 --> 01:12:03.480
I mean, you are not seeing all of it.
我是说，你们看到的并不是全部。

1615
01:12:03.600 --> 01:12:05.360
He went for so long.
他演了很长时间。

1616
01:12:05.580 --> 01:12:09.160
And I remember we were cracking up and we were just like, get it.
我记得我们当时笑得不行，心里都在想，快点演完吧。

1617
01:12:09.260 --> 01:12:11.160
Like as a group, we're like, no, get it together.
我们整个剧组都在想，不行，得控制住。

1618
01:12:11.340 --> 01:12:12.160
These are too good.
这些梗太棒了。

1619
01:12:12.700 --> 01:12:13.180
Ruin these.
别把这些给毁了。

1620
01:12:13.800 --> 01:12:19.200
Well, while all this is happening at the office, Dwight has gone to visit Meredith.
好了，当办公室里发生这一切的时候，德怀特去探望梅雷迪思了。

1621
01:12:19.780 --> 01:12:31.580
And he has this talking head where he's saying, as he's sitting next to her, that sometimes the best thing to do is to put an animal out of its misery.
他有一个对着镜头的独白，当时他坐在她旁边，说有时候最好的办法就是让动物从痛苦中解脱。

1622
01:12:31.960 --> 01:12:32.820
He's a farmer.
他是个农场主嘛。

1623
01:12:33.060 --> 01:12:33.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1624
01:12:33.440 --> 01:12:38.780
You could power a small fan for two days with the amount of electricity Meredith is hooked up to.
梅雷迪思身上连着的那些医疗设备所消耗的电量，足够带动一个小风扇转两天了。

1625
01:12:39.580 --> 01:12:53.800
I have to say, please, if you go back to rewatch this episode, during this speech by Dwight next to Meredith's bedside, please look at the woman in the bed on the other side.
我必须说，拜托，如果你回头重看这一集，在德怀特于梅雷迪思床边发表这段演说时，请留意一下另一边床上的那位女士。

1626
01:12:53.800 --> 01:12:54.680
Okay.
好的。

1627
01:12:55.020 --> 01:12:55.280
Okay.
好的。

1628
01:12:55.740 --> 01:12:57.060
Over Dwight's shoulder.
就在德怀特的肩膀后面。

1629
01:12:58.040 --> 01:12:59.120
That's all I'm going to say.
我只能说这么多了。

1630
01:12:59.240 --> 01:13:02.240
Just enjoy that performance the next time you watch this scene.
下次看这一幕时，好好欣赏她的表演吧。

1631
01:13:02.880 --> 01:13:03.880
It's wonderful.
那真是太精彩了。

1632
01:13:03.880 --> 01:13:05.360
Oh, my God, Jenna.
天哪，珍娜。

1633
01:13:05.720 --> 01:13:09.040
When we were all crammed around Kate's bed, that woman was there.
当我们都挤在凯特的床边时，那位女士就在那儿。

1634
01:13:10.260 --> 01:13:15.500
I swear, that woman, it was like she was a real patient.
我发誓，那位女士，感觉她就像个真正的病人一样。

1635
01:13:16.400 --> 01:13:21.380
She let out some kind of noise, and I thought we were all going to shit our pants.
她发出了一种声音，我当时以为我们都要吓尿了。

1636
01:13:22.260 --> 01:13:27.800
She was a background actor, but she was so real.
她只是个背景演员，但她演得太真实了。

1637
01:13:27.800 --> 01:13:36.320
Well, she literally, while we were standing there one time, went, like, I think they told her to maybe make a moaning sound.
有一次我们站在那儿的时候，她真的，我想他们可能让她发出一点呻吟声。

1638
01:13:36.580 --> 01:13:36.860
Yeah.
是啊。

1639
01:13:36.980 --> 01:13:40.180
And her interpretation of that, we went loopy.
而她对那个要求的演绎，让我们都快疯了。

1640
01:13:40.640 --> 01:13:43.820
Well, watch her in the background of the scene because she's excellent.
好好看看背景里的她，因为她演得太棒了。

1641
01:13:44.100 --> 01:13:47.500
So now the doctor comes in, and Dwight has some questions for him.
现在医生进来了，德怀特有一些问题要问他。

1642
01:13:47.820 --> 01:13:51.820
And you and I both know that this is our writer, Justin Spitzer.
你我都清楚，这位医生就是我们的编剧贾斯汀·斯皮策。

1643
01:13:53.400 --> 01:13:57.840
Yes, creator of some of your favorite Dwightisms, Justin Spitzer.
没错，他还是你最喜欢的那些“德怀特语录”的创作者，贾斯汀·斯皮策。

1644
01:13:58.100 --> 01:14:00.220
And the creator of the show, Superstore.
也是剧集《爆笑超市》的创作者。

1645
01:14:00.620 --> 01:14:05.820
Well, I reached out to Justin, and he told me that he got this role after reading the part in the table read.
我联系了贾斯汀，他告诉我，他是在剧本围读会上读了这个角色后才得到这个演出的。

1646
01:14:06.800 --> 01:14:08.360
That he made Greg laugh.
因为他把格雷格逗笑了。

1647
01:14:08.500 --> 01:14:10.720
Which Paul Lieberstein has shared that this would happen.
保罗·利伯斯坦曾分享过，这种情况时有发生。

1648
01:14:10.720 --> 01:14:14.580
They wouldn't have some of the roles cast, and they would have writers read them.
有些角色还没定演员，他们就会让编剧来读。

1649
01:14:14.740 --> 01:14:20.420
And if a writer read a part, get ready, because there was a good chance Greg was going to put you in the show.
如果编剧读了某个角色，那就做好准备吧，因为格雷格很有可能会让你在剧中出演。

1650
01:14:20.420 --> 01:14:29.780
Well, he also told me that the look he gives to camera was actually him misunderstanding a piece of direction from Greg.
他还告诉我，他看向镜头的那个眼神，其实是因为他误解了格雷格给出的一个指令。

1651
01:14:30.020 --> 01:14:35.680
That Greg did not intend him to, like, perform that line to the camera as, like, a little joke.
格雷格并不是想让他对着镜头说那句台词，就像是开个小玩笑一样。

1652
01:14:35.680 --> 01:14:37.360
Like, oh, so that's where it went.
就像是，噢，原来它去那儿了。

1653
01:14:37.360 --> 01:14:39.020
He's talking about Meredith's uterus.
他在谈论梅雷迪思的子宫。

1654
01:14:39.120 --> 01:14:39.320
Yeah.
没错。

1655
01:14:40.920 --> 01:14:42.740
But Greg left it in.
但格雷格把它留在了片子里。

1656
01:14:42.860 --> 01:14:43.760
I liked it.
我挺喜欢的。

1657
01:14:43.980 --> 01:14:45.100
I liked it, too.
我也挺喜欢的。

1658
01:14:45.100 --> 01:14:46.640
But he said that was not the intention.
但他说了那并非本意。

1659
01:14:46.640 --> 01:14:47.660
That was a mistake.
那是个失误。

1660
01:14:47.660 --> 01:15:00.720
Well, we learn in this scene that Meredith has been bitten by a bat, which we knew, but not only by a bat, but recently by a raccoon and a rat.
嗯，我们在这一幕中得知梅雷迪思被蝙蝠咬了，这点我们早就知道，但不仅是被蝙蝠咬，最近还被浣熊和老鼠咬过。

1661
01:15:00.960 --> 01:15:02.240
What the hell, Meredith?
搞什么鬼，梅雷迪思？

1662
01:15:02.840 --> 01:15:04.260
What is she doing?
她到底在干什么？

1663
01:15:04.640 --> 01:15:07.580
Honestly, a few of those animals could just live in her van.
说实话，其中几只动物完全可以直接住在她的货车里。

1664
01:15:08.100 --> 01:15:08.960
Meredith's van.
梅雷迪思的货车。

1665
01:15:09.140 --> 01:15:09.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1666
01:15:09.440 --> 01:15:15.500
Well, when Dwight comes back from the hospital, he fills Michael in on all of this.
好吧，当德怀特从医院回来时，他把这一切都告诉了迈克尔。

1667
01:15:15.680 --> 01:15:21.060
He says, you know, it turns out Meredith had been exposed to rabies.
他说，你知道，原来梅雷迪思接触过狂犬病毒。

1668
01:15:21.340 --> 01:15:22.720
Michael's like, ding, ding, ding, ding, ding.
迈克尔就像是，叮，叮，叮，叮，叮。

1669
01:15:23.600 --> 01:15:29.180
And that going to the hospital might have saved her life because she got a rabies vaccine.
而且去医院可能救了她的命，因为她接种了狂犬疫苗。

1670
01:15:29.360 --> 01:15:31.540
That is all Michael needed to hear.
这就是迈克尔需要听到的全部内容。

1671
01:15:32.340 --> 01:15:36.820
He hit her with a car and saved her life.
他开车撞了她，却救了她的命。

1672
01:15:37.240 --> 01:15:37.960
Yes.
没错。

1673
01:15:38.220 --> 01:15:46.260
Now, he also says in this scene, Dwight says, the only way to treat rabies is to start treatment before the symptoms start.
现在，他在这一幕中还说，德怀特说，治疗狂犬病的唯一方法是在症状出现前就开始治疗。

1674
01:15:47.080 --> 01:15:48.580
Well, I looked it up.
嗯，我查过了。

1675
01:15:48.780 --> 01:15:49.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1676
01:15:49.560 --> 01:15:50.800
This is true.
这是真的。

1677
01:15:51.520 --> 01:15:58.660
Did you know, Angela, that nearly 100% of people who develop symptoms die from rabies?
安吉拉，你知道吗，几乎100%出现症状的人都会死于狂犬病？

1678
01:15:59.240 --> 01:15:59.960
Die.
死亡。

1679
01:16:00.660 --> 01:16:03.180
It cannot be cured once you get it.
一旦感染就无法治愈。

1680
01:16:03.300 --> 01:16:04.360
I did not know that.
我不知道这一点。

1681
01:16:04.980 --> 01:16:05.380
Yes.
是的。

1682
01:16:05.560 --> 01:16:10.640
So this is why you have to seek treatment immediately if you are ever bitten by an animal.
所以这就是为什么如果你被动物咬伤，必须立即寻求治疗。

1683
01:16:10.780 --> 01:16:12.760
And a lot of animals can carry rabies.
而且很多动物都可能携带狂犬病毒。

1684
01:16:12.900 --> 01:16:22.940
But since I looked it up, I'll let you know that in the United States, the most likely way to transmit rabies is through bats, coyotes, foxes, raccoons, and skunks.
但既然我查过了，我就告诉你，在美国，传播狂犬病最常见的方式是通过蝙蝠、郊狼、狐狸、浣熊和臭鼬。

1685
01:16:23.940 --> 01:16:27.540
In Africa and Southeast Asia, it is stray dogs.
在非洲和东南亚，则是流浪狗。

1686
01:16:27.740 --> 01:16:28.740
I mean, what about monkeys?
我是说，猴子呢？

1687
01:16:28.740 --> 01:16:34.540
There's parts of, like, Indonesia, like, if you go up to Ubud, like, there's monkeys, like, all over the place.
像印度尼西亚的一些地方，比如如果你去乌布，到处都是猴子。

1688
01:16:34.660 --> 01:16:34.920
Any animal bite.
任何动物咬伤。

1689
01:16:35.080 --> 01:16:37.900
If you get bitten by any animal, just go.
如果你被任何动物咬了，直接去医院。

1690
01:16:38.220 --> 01:16:40.080
Go get a rabies vaccine.
去打狂犬疫苗。

1691
01:16:40.540 --> 01:16:41.720
It also said—
上面还说——

1692
01:16:41.720 --> 01:16:42.740
What about squirrels?
松鼠呢？

1693
01:16:43.900 --> 01:16:44.380
Yes!
是的！

1694
01:16:44.640 --> 01:16:45.560
Any animal.
任何动物。

1695
01:16:45.800 --> 01:16:47.580
If any animal bites you.
如果任何动物咬了你。

1696
01:16:47.580 --> 01:16:52.680
I'm just telling you the animals that are most likely to carry rabies in these locations.
我只是在告诉你这些地方最容易携带狂犬病毒的动物。

1697
01:16:52.680 --> 01:16:55.500
But any animal can give it to you.
但任何动物都可能传染给你。

1698
01:16:55.600 --> 01:16:56.780
Is a mongoose on the list?
猫鼬在名单上吗？

1699
01:16:58.420 --> 01:17:00.740
Is a mongoose any animal?
猫鼬算任何动物吗？

1700
01:17:02.540 --> 01:17:05.380
I'm just messing with you, but it's been really fun.
我只是在逗你玩，但这真的很有趣。

1701
01:17:08.000 --> 01:17:11.800
Well, listen, here is the thing that I found most interesting.
听着，这是我发现最有趣的一点。

1702
01:17:11.800 --> 01:17:13.840
This is from the Mayo Clinic website.
这是来自梅奥诊所网站的内容。

1703
01:17:14.140 --> 01:17:15.220
Here's what it says.
上面是这么说的。

1704
01:17:15.380 --> 01:17:15.760
Okay.
好的。

1705
01:17:16.380 --> 01:17:19.060
If you wake up in the morning—
如果你早上醒来——

1706
01:17:19.060 --> 01:17:19.240
Okay.
好的。

1707
01:17:19.700 --> 01:17:21.540
—and there's a bat in your room—
——发现房间里有一只蝙蝠——

1708
01:17:21.540 --> 01:17:21.900
Okay.
好的。

1709
01:17:22.560 --> 01:17:24.420
